WEBVTT

01:03.605 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:07.650 --> 01:09.903
Is he a spy? He's not, is he?

01:10.487 --> 01:12.989
I heard he was born and raised in Busan.

01:13.073 --> 01:13.990
Hey, Kim.

01:14.574 --> 01:16.701
The kid doesn't decide what he is.

01:17.202 --> 01:18.828
That's for Namsan CIA to decide.

01:22.165 --> 01:24.542
You finished the food. Were you hungry?

01:27.045 --> 01:28.254
Keep your head down.

01:28.922 --> 01:30.507
Head down. Is this a theater?

01:30.590 --> 01:33.343
These kids run away
because the government feeds them.

01:33.426 --> 01:36.679
These punks with their heads full of crap
need to be sent to Namsan.

01:36.763 --> 01:38.973
Putting them behind bars
would be patriotic.

01:43.686 --> 01:45.980
How sweet. They're in love.

01:49.943 --> 01:51.820
Have you lost your mind, kid?

01:53.238 --> 01:55.115
You're in the big city now, Jeju boy.

01:55.198 --> 01:56.491
Why roll up your sleeves?

01:56.574 --> 02:00.370
How dare you act tough
in front of a big-city senior officer!

02:00.453 --> 02:02.205
-You punk!
-Are you a lord?

02:07.043 --> 02:10.672
If you hit us, must we take it?
If you send us to Namsan, must we go?

02:10.755 --> 02:13.508
How sweet. Double trouble.

02:13.591 --> 02:17.053
Can you believe this?
These little punks are shameless!

02:17.137 --> 02:17.971
So what if I am?

02:18.054 --> 02:21.057
Is it illegal? Will I get locked up?
Am I going to Namsan?

02:21.558 --> 02:22.809
You smoke, don't you?

02:23.601 --> 02:25.937
You smoke, and you wear miniskirts?

02:26.020 --> 02:27.564
Am I going to Namsan for that?

02:28.481 --> 02:30.567
That lady reported us as runaways, right?

02:30.650 --> 02:33.153
She couldn't say anything else
because she felt guilty.

02:33.236 --> 02:36.364
What else? Did you steal something?
You caused more trouble, right?

02:36.447 --> 02:39.659
We're not being held here
because we hit anyone or stole anything.

02:39.742 --> 02:44.497
We're minors who need the protection
of the Busan Police.

02:44.581 --> 02:45.415
That's why

02:46.457 --> 02:49.419
we're also quietly waiting
for our guardians, so--

02:49.502 --> 02:52.046
-Shall we serve you?
-Don't hit him in the head!

02:57.093 --> 02:59.512
Send this girl to the National Assembly.

03:00.096 --> 03:01.139
Oh man.

03:01.222 --> 03:04.100
I didn't know Romeo and Juliet
were from Jeju.

03:04.851 --> 03:06.477
Aren't you calling your mothers?

03:06.561 --> 03:07.604
They don't need to.

03:07.687 --> 03:10.190
The woman camping out front
is the boy's mother.

03:11.107 --> 03:12.192
What?

03:12.775 --> 03:14.235
This one is handsome.

03:15.361 --> 03:16.821
This one is vixen-like.

03:18.031 --> 03:18.907
Here she comes.

03:20.992 --> 03:21.826
Mom.

03:25.622 --> 03:26.456
Mom.

03:31.211 --> 03:34.589
-Where's the bag? Where's my stuff?
-What?

03:35.256 --> 03:36.257
Where's my jewelry?

03:40.053 --> 03:41.721
My gold… Good grief!

03:42.764 --> 03:44.390
Where's my gold frog?

03:44.474 --> 03:45.975
Where's my gold frog?

03:58.988 --> 03:59.822
Is it real?

03:59.906 --> 04:01.574
It is real gold, isn't it?

04:03.451 --> 04:04.285
It is.

04:06.579 --> 04:08.748
He always does too much.

04:08.831 --> 04:11.209
He's like this
for every wedding anniversary.

04:11.292 --> 04:13.962
He just can't wait to buy me gifts
on special days.

04:14.629 --> 04:15.463
Is that so?

04:17.674 --> 04:21.052
Our cabinet is chock-full of jewelry.

04:21.928 --> 04:23.972
I'm clearing out anything out of style.

04:24.597 --> 04:25.682
Give me a good price.

04:26.182 --> 04:27.016
Is that so?

04:27.684 --> 04:30.311
You gave me a good price
for the jewelry last time.

04:30.812 --> 04:33.356
You came last summer
and said it was your anniversary.

04:34.023 --> 04:36.609
Isn't your anniversary in the summer?

04:37.443 --> 04:40.196
Your husband got you a gold bracelet
back then, right?

04:42.865 --> 04:45.660
No, it's in the spring.

04:47.245 --> 04:48.371
Is that so?

04:50.039 --> 04:51.040
What if it is?

04:52.208 --> 04:53.293
Is that a problem?

04:54.961 --> 04:56.045
Hello.

04:56.713 --> 04:58.798
-How much is it?
-300 won.

04:58.881 --> 04:59.966
-Give it to me.
-Okay.

05:00.049 --> 05:01.718
-No, give it to me.
-To me.

05:03.303 --> 05:04.220
Give it to me.

05:04.971 --> 05:06.389
Just give it to me.

05:06.472 --> 05:09.225
No, don't give it to her.
Just give it to me.

05:09.309 --> 05:11.686
Hey, I'm the owner. Why would he pay you?

05:11.769 --> 05:14.397
-Is this your inn?
-It's my money anyway.

05:14.480 --> 05:18.484
This woman stole my bag,
so I'm taking whatever I can from her.

05:18.568 --> 05:19.402
No. Give it to me.

05:19.485 --> 05:20.820
I'll come back later.

05:20.903 --> 05:22.655
Wait, hold on!

05:22.739 --> 05:24.449
Where are you going? Wait…

05:29.662 --> 05:30.747
Just go away.

05:31.539 --> 05:32.832
Gonna stay all night?

05:34.250 --> 05:37.086
Hey, you know
why there are no thieves in Jeju?

05:37.170 --> 05:39.047
Why? Are Jeju folks epically generous?

05:39.130 --> 05:42.550
We wear them down.
We keep going until they're sick of it.

05:42.633 --> 05:45.094
It's the thief, not the victim,
who ends up cracking

05:45.178 --> 05:47.388
because we wear them down.

05:49.682 --> 05:52.101
Wow, you lunatic.

05:52.185 --> 05:53.603
For Christ's sake.

05:54.103 --> 05:55.355
You're a lunatic!

05:55.438 --> 05:57.482
An absolute lunatic!

05:57.982 --> 06:00.360
Completely out of your damn mind!

06:00.943 --> 06:04.364
I'm taking what I'm owed, no matter what.

06:04.447 --> 06:08.451
I'll be here day and night
until I get what my gold toad is worth.

06:08.534 --> 06:10.953
What? Did you say gold toad?

06:12.246 --> 06:13.664
Give me my gold toad.

06:13.748 --> 06:14.749
Hey.

06:15.625 --> 06:17.460
So the gold frog is a gold toad now?

06:17.543 --> 06:18.628
You're the thief--

06:20.588 --> 06:22.215
Do you have a frog's brain?

06:22.298 --> 06:24.884
What can you do?
You should give her the gold frog back.

06:26.677 --> 06:29.305
It's too late now.
Give me a gold toad now.

06:30.473 --> 06:33.017
You're one brazen robber, aren't you?

06:33.101 --> 06:34.936
I bet you've got a criminal record.

06:35.019 --> 06:36.270
You do, don't you?

06:36.354 --> 06:37.897
Should we call the cops?

06:37.980 --> 06:40.775
-Should we call the cops?
-Ma'am!

06:40.858 --> 06:43.111
-Ma'am!
-What the hell?

06:46.322 --> 06:49.325
Why did you go to the jewelry store? Why?

06:53.454 --> 06:55.748
This will be your tenth offense.

06:56.416 --> 06:58.292
Think of your child, will you?

06:58.793 --> 06:59.794
Let's go.

06:59.877 --> 07:02.296
Don't let anyone from Jeju stay
while I'm away.

07:03.172 --> 07:04.674
Take her away.

07:04.757 --> 07:05.800
Get off me!

07:05.883 --> 07:07.844
This is her tenth offense?

07:08.428 --> 07:11.389
Wow, she's got some nerve.

07:24.235 --> 07:26.487
Hey, you better pay for the fan!

07:27.071 --> 07:28.114
Pay for the fan!

07:28.197 --> 07:30.324
Were you performing circus acts in there?

07:30.408 --> 07:32.076
How did you even manage to break it?

07:32.160 --> 07:33.786
Well done! Great job!

07:34.412 --> 07:35.663
Hey, stop pushing me!

07:44.755 --> 07:46.299
My goodness.

07:53.848 --> 07:55.766
Did you buy the tofu already?

07:56.767 --> 07:57.602
No.

07:58.186 --> 07:59.687
I didn't buy it.

07:59.770 --> 08:01.105
The lady bought it for us.

08:06.486 --> 08:09.906
What about your first birthday rings?
You didn't bring them with you?

08:10.406 --> 08:11.699
Didn't you take them too?

08:11.782 --> 08:13.701
Everything we took was in the bag.

08:17.038 --> 08:18.623
Your dad… That worthless mutt.

08:19.373 --> 08:20.708
Dogs are better

08:20.791 --> 08:23.377
than both you and your father.

08:28.174 --> 08:29.550
Ae-sun, let's go home.

08:33.346 --> 08:35.473
You've really done it this time, Ae-sun.

08:35.556 --> 08:38.267
YESTERDAY WAS YOUR SPRING

08:38.351 --> 08:40.520
You've really done it, Ae-sun.

08:41.103 --> 08:42.313
FACULTY OFFICE

08:48.653 --> 08:50.363
She should've done it on her own.

08:50.446 --> 08:52.573
Why drag down
another family's eldest grandson?

08:58.162 --> 09:00.957
I heard he's one
of the top four athletes in Jeju.

09:01.040 --> 09:03.793
Well, she's the poet of class eight.

09:03.876 --> 09:05.294
Poet, my foot.

09:05.795 --> 09:08.172
She wants to be a poet,
but dating is the best she can do?

09:25.231 --> 09:28.651
POEMS OF YU CHI-HWAN
HANDKERCHIEF OF ETERNAL NOSTALGIA

09:34.448 --> 09:36.200
EXPULSION NOTICE
OH AE-SUN

09:36.284 --> 09:40.371
DUE TO AN UNAUTHORIZED RUNAWAY
AND DISRUPTIVE BEHAVIOR

09:42.164 --> 09:44.709
You've completely ruined your life!

09:45.293 --> 09:48.379
People exaggerate everything
on this island.

09:48.462 --> 09:51.090
I can't even show my face
at the wholesale market.

09:51.173 --> 09:54.010
You've brought shame to our family!

09:54.093 --> 09:55.303
And Jong-gu made us proud?

09:56.846 --> 09:58.472
How can you compare him to her?

09:58.556 --> 10:02.935
A man can lose his land or his home
while running a business.

10:03.019 --> 10:04.979
Why do you keep bringing him up?

10:05.062 --> 10:07.440
Did he run a business? He played cards.

10:08.649 --> 10:09.942
So now what?

10:10.026 --> 10:12.653
What will you do now?
You won't go to the factory.

10:12.737 --> 10:15.740
You can't get married.
Will you die a spinster in this house?

10:21.579 --> 10:24.498
What about him? What did that brat say?

10:29.128 --> 10:32.298
Don't you see your grandmother,
who raised you since you were a baby?

10:32.381 --> 10:34.884
Do you only care about yourself?

10:34.967 --> 10:36.552
How can I face our ancestors?

10:36.636 --> 10:40.056
I'm the one marrying her,
not our ancestors.

10:43.934 --> 10:45.561
What will we say to our ancestors?

10:45.645 --> 10:48.981
That our filial son brought home
an orphan wife, a middle school graduate?

10:49.774 --> 10:53.361
Who brings a middle school graduate
into a noble family as a daughter-in-law?

10:53.861 --> 10:55.529
Why is she a middle school graduate?

10:55.613 --> 10:56.530
What did you expect?

10:56.614 --> 10:59.909
That the school would just give her
a diploma after she eloped at night?

11:01.202 --> 11:03.079
Just go beg there!

11:03.704 --> 11:06.165
Go beg there
so you can become their daughter-in-law.

11:06.248 --> 11:08.459
The whole island knows about their affair.

11:08.542 --> 11:10.628
She's lost any chance
of having a proper marriage.

11:10.711 --> 11:12.213
She can't marry Gwan-sik either.

11:12.296 --> 11:14.256
His grandmother almost fainted.

11:15.091 --> 11:19.428
Wow, Oh Ae-sun.
Heck of a relationship you've got there.

11:19.512 --> 11:22.765
Gambling away your whole life
by eloping at night.

11:25.184 --> 11:26.435
I've only been suspended.

11:26.519 --> 11:28.437
Wow, congratulations.

11:28.521 --> 11:29.855
But why was she the only one

11:31.774 --> 11:32.900
who got expelled?

11:32.983 --> 11:35.611
Middle school graduates can't even solder.

11:35.695 --> 11:36.654
Damn it.

11:36.737 --> 11:37.905
Why was only Ae-sun…

11:37.988 --> 11:39.532
Do you really not know?

11:39.615 --> 11:41.075
It might take two to tango,

11:41.158 --> 11:42.952
but the boy gets called a hero

11:43.035 --> 11:45.705
while the girl's love
gets branded shameless.

11:45.788 --> 11:48.749
Did you ruin her life
without knowing better?

11:49.542 --> 11:50.876
It was my idea.

11:51.585 --> 11:53.087
That fool just followed along.

11:53.879 --> 11:54.922
We should be so proud!

11:56.716 --> 11:58.926
Remove him from the family registry!

12:00.010 --> 12:01.512
No one's punishing my kid!

12:01.595 --> 12:03.264
Ae-sun should be punished.

12:03.931 --> 12:06.350
You don't burn the whole house down
over one maggot.

12:06.434 --> 12:09.895
Why punish someone else's kid?
Our son is the one who's crazy about her.

12:09.979 --> 12:14.650
Seriously, I'm going to take that girl,
scold her, and pinch her, then…

12:14.734 --> 12:15.818
Come on!

12:15.901 --> 12:17.403
Did that work last time?

12:17.486 --> 12:20.114
What good did pulling my hair do?

12:20.197 --> 12:22.658
You want me to lose my grandson
under my nose too?!

12:24.535 --> 12:27.288
You don't catch a chicken
by chasing it with a stick.

12:27.371 --> 12:28.998
You lure it with a worm.

12:29.498 --> 12:30.916
You have to wheedle them.

12:31.000 --> 12:33.919
If you chase them, they'll run miles away.

12:35.755 --> 12:39.133
How could they use a spoon
to lock you away? Seriously.

12:40.885 --> 12:41.844
Oh dear.

12:44.221 --> 12:45.222
Goodness me.

12:45.931 --> 12:48.350
Have you had something to eat?

12:48.851 --> 12:49.769
Yes.

12:50.436 --> 12:53.564
I never skip meals.

12:56.025 --> 12:57.151
I see.

12:57.234 --> 12:58.819
Well, that's good to hear.

12:58.903 --> 13:01.739
Gwan-sik hasn't been able to eat a thing.

13:01.822 --> 13:04.033
Is he on a hunger strike?

13:04.116 --> 13:05.826
You know he'd never do that.

13:05.910 --> 13:09.038
His father told me not to feed him
a single grain of rice.

13:12.500 --> 13:16.378
Ae-sun, even though I want to help,

13:16.462 --> 13:20.716
you know I can't go against
his grandmother, don't you?

13:21.258 --> 13:26.514
I married into this tiresome Yang family,
and I'm still paying the price for it.

13:27.097 --> 13:29.266
You know how stubborn the Yangs are.

13:29.350 --> 13:33.479
Remember how Gwan-sik stole fish from us
to give to you every day for ten years?

13:35.356 --> 13:37.900
I gave your family cabbages
from time to time too.

13:40.569 --> 13:42.863
Where do you think he gets it from?

13:42.947 --> 13:44.990
He gets it from his father.

13:45.074 --> 13:49.662
His father is even willing
to sever ties with him for good.

13:50.579 --> 13:51.622
Goodness.

13:52.289 --> 13:54.792
That's how narrow-minded he is.

13:56.210 --> 14:00.130
I was once so crazy about him,
I even eloped with him at night.

14:00.214 --> 14:02.675
But you can't expect
to live on love forever.

14:03.342 --> 14:07.680
Right up until the wedding,
they'll tell you that you're the only one.

14:08.305 --> 14:12.893
But once married, they forget you.
They're just devoted to their mothers.

14:14.520 --> 14:16.647
You wait and see, okay?

14:17.439 --> 14:20.359
You'll end up alone
in our family for sure.

14:23.988 --> 14:26.574
-Well…
-Yeah, what is it?

14:28.909 --> 14:32.454
Can I ask you something?

14:51.307 --> 14:54.977
We're in a tight spot financially,
and it's been pretty unsettling for us.

14:55.978 --> 14:58.147
We can't even offer your family
a silver spoon.

14:58.230 --> 15:00.024
Still, I'd never let her starve.

15:01.400 --> 15:03.903
What about your family?
Do they approve of her?

15:04.820 --> 15:05.946
Can you beat a shaman?

15:06.614 --> 15:08.407
Your shaman grandma said

15:08.490 --> 15:11.368
that Ae-sun was bound
to her widow mother's spirit.

15:12.077 --> 15:15.164
Everyone here worships the Dragon King
rather than God or Buddha.

15:15.873 --> 15:17.833
No one can stand up to a shaman.

15:19.043 --> 15:21.754
Ae-sun will be living with me,
not my grandmother.

15:22.254 --> 15:23.839
I'll keep Ae-sun safe from her.

15:23.923 --> 15:26.342
So what? Are you planning on moving out?

15:26.425 --> 15:27.801
You have a home in your name?

15:30.179 --> 15:32.473
Who do you think you are,
taking care of me?

15:32.556 --> 15:34.725
Do you think I'm spoiled fish
you can get cheap?

15:35.267 --> 15:37.895
You had her sleep in a room
with fermented soybean bricks?

15:37.978 --> 15:41.440
I won't do it.
It makes me feel small and cheap. No way.

15:41.523 --> 15:42.691
But I want to.

15:42.775 --> 15:45.444
Why? You think
I can't get married unless it's to you?

15:46.278 --> 15:49.156
I'm going to marry a richer,
more handsome man,

15:49.239 --> 15:50.699
a son less precious than you!

15:50.783 --> 15:52.576
Go on, then. Get married.

15:52.660 --> 15:53.661
Take anyone you can!

15:53.744 --> 15:55.996
I won't do it. I'll never marry you.

15:56.080 --> 15:58.248
See if I ever marry you. Just watch me!

16:09.635 --> 16:11.470
Hey! Bring some tea here.

16:12.221 --> 16:15.099
-Miss Ko, serve him some tea.
-Yes, ma'am.

16:15.683 --> 16:17.101
Hello, sir.

16:17.184 --> 16:20.312
So you raised two siblings
all on your own?

16:22.147 --> 16:25.859
That experience
is the main reason I approved of you.

16:26.568 --> 16:27.403
I see.

16:42.960 --> 16:46.088
I heard you really wanted
a man from Seoul.

16:48.799 --> 16:52.219
I'm… pretty much from Seoul.

16:53.387 --> 16:55.264
Right after Korea's liberation,

16:55.347 --> 16:57.725
my wealthy family sent me
to study in Seoul.

16:58.600 --> 17:01.020
If I hadn't married and moved down here,

17:01.770 --> 17:03.272
I could've been a man of power.

17:07.818 --> 17:10.112
At the beginning of my first marriage…

17:11.947 --> 17:13.741
Am I getting that tea anytime today?

17:23.459 --> 17:25.377
Don't worry about what I think.

17:26.003 --> 17:28.338
Love isn't a crime, after all.

17:30.424 --> 17:35.012
I heard a few things
about your past through the grapevine.

17:35.095 --> 17:36.013
But today,

17:37.473 --> 17:39.475
I just took the plunge and came out.

17:41.101 --> 17:45.105
I've crossed the Pacific many times,
so handling a small flaw is no big deal.

17:45.606 --> 17:48.776
I'm more of a Seoul type.
I don't care about things like that.

17:50.194 --> 17:52.571
They say remarriages
work out better for both.

17:52.654 --> 17:54.698
It takes one to know one, you know.

17:54.782 --> 17:58.494
It'd be very demanding to marry someone
who'd never been married.

17:59.078 --> 18:00.788
That would give me a headache.

18:07.836 --> 18:10.297
Are you going to drink that thing?
It cost 50 won.

18:15.594 --> 18:17.262
Sure, he's been married before,

18:17.346 --> 18:19.098
but he owns boats.

18:19.640 --> 18:21.517
Not just one.

18:21.600 --> 18:24.853
To go on a boat in Dodong-ri,
you have to use one of his family's.

18:27.064 --> 18:28.482
If you really want,

18:28.982 --> 18:32.194
I heard he'll try to send you to college
within ten years.

18:33.320 --> 18:34.905
If you do well,

18:35.447 --> 18:38.867
he might even think about
publishing your poetry book.

18:41.161 --> 18:42.538
It's only two children, so…

18:44.873 --> 18:46.375
At least it's not three.

18:50.379 --> 18:53.048
I guess I was born to be a maid.

18:54.675 --> 18:55.551
My goodness.

18:57.553 --> 18:59.888
The spring rain is lasting a long time.

19:03.600 --> 19:05.561
Maybe it's my mom crying.

19:09.481 --> 19:12.317
Maybe she's crying
because I'm getting married like this.

19:25.622 --> 19:28.792
Gwang-rye will be turning in her grave!

19:30.085 --> 19:34.381
You've totally ruined a young girl's life,
and you still have an appetite?

19:34.464 --> 19:37.384
If you're so sad about her,
give her your son.

19:37.467 --> 19:38.510
How does that sound?

19:38.594 --> 19:40.971
No way is she marrying
a man who's been married!

19:41.054 --> 19:44.725
Both families are so determined
to get rid of Ae-sun.

19:45.475 --> 19:46.476
Mak-cheon.

19:46.560 --> 19:48.312
You may perform rituals,

19:48.395 --> 19:50.814
but you have no right
to scold other families.

19:51.398 --> 19:53.275
If she marries that man,

19:53.358 --> 19:55.903
I won't believe in your Dragon King
or the spirits.

19:55.986 --> 19:58.238
Being good should pay off.

19:58.322 --> 19:59.781
Being good should pay!

19:59.865 --> 20:01.617
Stop talking already!

20:02.201 --> 20:03.452
Is Ae-sun getting married?

20:07.706 --> 20:09.666
MADAM BAEK GI-NAM'S 60TH BIRTHDAY

20:14.796 --> 20:18.217
Are you regifting that gift set
to my family?

20:18.717 --> 20:20.135
This is American.

20:22.638 --> 20:24.348
Only it's made in Korea.

20:24.973 --> 20:27.935
It's all the same once you eat it.

20:28.018 --> 20:30.520
I despise all these pointless formalities.

20:31.605 --> 20:35.943
The whole wedding business
is just another meaningless formality.

20:36.026 --> 20:38.111
It's just a way of robbing people.

20:42.366 --> 20:46.453
Honestly, white dresses
are for first weddings.

20:47.037 --> 20:49.414
Let's just wear formal clothes
and take some photos.

20:49.498 --> 20:52.417
Technically, it's not the first
for either of us anyway.

20:54.419 --> 20:56.171
Speaking of which,

20:57.005 --> 20:59.591
I was personally curious about something.

21:00.467 --> 21:01.343
Well…

21:04.346 --> 21:05.180
About Busan.

21:10.477 --> 21:12.271
Does your mother know about this?

21:14.064 --> 21:17.651
Good heavens.
You must've cleared out your entire store.

21:17.734 --> 21:20.153
-Goodness.
-This is as good as theft.

21:21.613 --> 21:23.031
I won't let Ae-sun starve either.

21:23.532 --> 21:25.742
I can give her a whole mackerel every day.

21:25.826 --> 21:27.703
We are no longer living in a time of war.

21:27.786 --> 21:29.121
People don't marry for food.

21:31.123 --> 21:33.875
Are you really her grandmother?
Are you really her uncle?

21:33.959 --> 21:37.296
I knew something was up
when you wouldn't give her any croakers!

21:37.379 --> 21:39.131
Why are you bringing up croakers?

21:39.214 --> 21:42.467
I heard he has already been married.
That he's 30!

21:43.051 --> 21:45.512
Why would you match Ae-sun
with a man like him?

21:45.595 --> 21:48.765
Even the actor Shin Seong-il
wouldn't be good enough for her!

21:48.849 --> 21:51.059
Why would a movie star want Ae-sun?

21:51.143 --> 21:54.187
Why would you throw away
a girl as pretty as Ae-sun?

21:57.607 --> 22:00.444
She's smart, well-spoken,

22:00.527 --> 22:02.029
and really cute.

22:03.071 --> 22:05.657
Why would you? Why?

22:06.908 --> 22:07.951
Keep on yapping.

22:13.915 --> 22:15.083
Let me take her.

22:15.167 --> 22:17.336
I've been giving her croakers for years

22:17.836 --> 22:19.921
and selling her cabbages all this time.

22:20.005 --> 22:22.507
I care about Ae-sun more than anyone else!

22:23.300 --> 22:25.927
More than you!
So why are you taking her from me?

22:26.011 --> 22:27.846
What do you want me to do?

22:27.929 --> 22:29.431
Should I put her on a leash?

22:29.514 --> 22:33.310
Should I put her on a leash
and drag her to marry you?

22:33.393 --> 22:35.479
She doesn't want to.
Who will change her mind?

22:36.063 --> 22:39.816
When a tame cow decides to rebel,
it won't budge.

22:40.567 --> 22:42.444
You can't force it to plow the field.

22:43.403 --> 22:44.988
What's wrong with her?

22:45.072 --> 22:46.656
Go ask your mother.

22:47.741 --> 22:49.743
Ask her how she convinced Ae-sun.

22:52.079 --> 22:53.997
You know, in Busan,

22:54.915 --> 22:58.502
were you caught the day you ran away
or some time later?

22:59.628 --> 23:03.673
I guess kids today will do what they want,
even if they don't stay the night.

23:04.174 --> 23:05.592
How about you, Captain?

23:07.636 --> 23:12.015
Did you separate from your wife
early in the marriage or some time later?

23:13.683 --> 23:14.518
Goddamn it!

23:16.978 --> 23:18.230
You've got a temper.

23:18.814 --> 23:20.690
Yes, I do.

23:21.358 --> 23:23.902
That's why I dislike rude people.

23:23.985 --> 23:26.822
Does that boy know this side of you?
And he still likes you?

23:26.905 --> 23:28.824
-It's why he likes me!
-Goddamn it!

23:29.741 --> 23:30.617
You little punk!

23:31.118 --> 23:33.453
Don't get in the way of this marriage!

23:33.537 --> 23:34.371
Darn it.

23:34.871 --> 23:35.747
It's a party now.

23:38.583 --> 23:40.544
Hey, kid. You little punk!

23:41.336 --> 23:42.921
What? What now?

23:43.004 --> 23:43.839
Let's go.

23:46.049 --> 23:47.050
Come on. Let's go!

23:48.301 --> 23:50.429
Where? Go where?

23:51.263 --> 23:52.222
Got anywhere to go?

23:53.515 --> 23:55.517
Goddamn it! Hey, you!

23:56.643 --> 23:59.146
How dare you be disrespectful
when a grown-up--

23:59.229 --> 24:00.480
Shut it, mister!

24:08.488 --> 24:09.739
Don't go. Marry me.

24:09.823 --> 24:11.741
You have the ring on, so that's it.

24:12.409 --> 24:14.536
What's it for? Can we live off it forever?

24:14.619 --> 24:16.872
Are we running away again?
To become thieves?

24:16.955 --> 24:18.373
Are you really marrying him?

24:20.792 --> 24:23.003
Why would you? Why?

24:23.086 --> 24:25.797
Yeah, he's remarrying and has two kids.

24:26.965 --> 24:29.301
But why would you? Why?

24:29.384 --> 24:31.386
Exactly! Why me? Why only me?

24:32.053 --> 24:33.430
Why do I get all the blame?

24:33.513 --> 24:36.516
Why was I the only one expelled?
Why am I the "shameless" one?

24:37.726 --> 24:38.810
It's over. All of it.

24:38.894 --> 24:40.645
College? Being a poet?

24:42.689 --> 24:44.107
It's all gone to crap.

24:44.941 --> 24:46.902
I can't even become a solderer now.

24:46.985 --> 24:48.320
I said I'd take care of you.

24:48.403 --> 24:50.405
-I've told you a million--
-But how?

24:51.323 --> 24:53.492
What have you done for me since I was ten?

24:53.575 --> 24:55.911
Give me mackerels? Croakers?

24:55.994 --> 24:56.870
I'm not a beggar!

24:56.953 --> 24:58.955
You were ten, but so was I.

24:59.789 --> 25:02.751
-What can a ten-year-old do?
-He said he'd do everything for me.

25:02.834 --> 25:05.295
He'll send me to college
and let me be a poet.

25:05.378 --> 25:06.213
I can do that too!

25:06.296 --> 25:09.049
I'll work on boats.
I'll lay bricks. Anything!

25:09.132 --> 25:10.967
No! I don't want you!

25:19.768 --> 25:23.688
Being with you would be like
always getting a losing roll.

25:26.775 --> 25:29.611
-What?
-I'm tired of having to be so willful.

25:29.694 --> 25:33.281
I'm sick of living with a family
that doesn't want me.

25:34.199 --> 25:38.620
I want to be rich too.
I want to live a comfortable life.

25:38.703 --> 25:41.790
If I marry you,
I'll just get even more mistreated.

25:42.290 --> 25:44.626
But if I marry him,
no one will speak badly of me.

25:44.709 --> 25:45.669
Not even you.

25:46.253 --> 25:49.422
Because you know everything.
You've seen it all. I've…

25:55.512 --> 25:56.680
I've…

25:58.682 --> 26:00.725
lived in shame my whole life.

26:01.434 --> 26:02.936
One of them is free.

26:03.436 --> 26:04.479
Did your mom say so?

26:05.272 --> 26:06.231
Did she say that?

26:06.314 --> 26:09.818
There are six people in the family,
but you only ever buy five.

26:09.901 --> 26:11.611
Do you make a fortune selling fish?

26:11.695 --> 26:13.280
Nosy little brat.

26:14.656 --> 26:16.449
That little punk.

26:19.286 --> 26:20.412
You've seen it all.

26:22.122 --> 26:23.123
I…

26:24.499 --> 26:26.668
I miss her so much.

26:27.335 --> 26:29.713
He told me to go to Busan.

26:29.796 --> 26:32.465
He told me to work at a factory!

26:32.549 --> 26:34.968
I don't have a home anymore.

26:36.595 --> 26:37.762
You know everything,

26:38.346 --> 26:40.265
and you want me to keep living like this?

26:43.268 --> 26:44.519
If I'm with you…

26:46.855 --> 26:49.024
I won't find happiness in marriage.

26:50.275 --> 26:52.527
Please let me live my life.

26:57.365 --> 26:58.950
Let me change the fate you pity so.

27:03.330 --> 27:04.331
Am I

27:04.998 --> 27:06.458
standing in your way?

27:13.840 --> 27:14.674
Gwan-sik.

27:17.385 --> 27:19.304
You have to leave so I can live my life.

27:20.889 --> 27:22.349
You have to leave…

27:24.559 --> 27:25.685
so I can live my life.

27:46.247 --> 27:48.875
For ages, she gazed
at her 18-year-old first love,

27:49.376 --> 27:51.836
whom she would never see again…

27:54.005 --> 27:57.759
and buried her pure love
in that yellow spring.

27:58.593 --> 28:00.345
Tearfully so.

28:01.304 --> 28:02.389
My ring.

28:09.187 --> 28:10.563
My ring.

28:21.658 --> 28:25.161
They say working in a field is rewarding,
but parenting never is.

28:26.413 --> 28:28.581
Of course you treat me differently.

28:28.665 --> 28:30.667
You'd never treat me like your own child.

28:31.501 --> 28:36.005
Every time she split a fried egg,
my portion was always smaller than yours.

28:36.089 --> 28:37.757
There you go again.

28:37.841 --> 28:40.343
Mom, why did you marry
into a family like this?

28:40.844 --> 28:43.263
I chose my own path.
I only have myself to blame.

28:44.222 --> 28:46.391
I wouldn't choose to live like you.

28:46.975 --> 28:48.184
No way. Never.

28:49.853 --> 28:52.439
I will marry a man from Seoul,
no matter what.

28:53.148 --> 28:56.401
Not a guy who doesn't even know
what "nostalgia" is.

28:56.484 --> 28:57.318
Never!

28:59.028 --> 29:02.115
That's right. You should "never."

29:04.534 --> 29:07.203
So do you regret it? Even a little?

29:09.289 --> 29:10.832
Of course not.

29:10.915 --> 29:13.918
If I hadn't met your father,
none of you would be here.

29:14.002 --> 29:15.754
No, not as a mom.

29:15.837 --> 29:16.921
As Oh Ae-sun.

29:20.508 --> 29:21.634
Just eat your chicken.

29:21.718 --> 29:23.386
What? Tell us.

29:24.179 --> 29:28.683
Do you, Oh Ae-sun, regret it?
Do you think about what could've been?

29:29.726 --> 29:30.935
Oh Ae-sun?

29:32.604 --> 29:33.897
Oh Ae-sun…

29:37.776 --> 29:39.861
was truly broken that spring.

30:14.062 --> 30:18.191
Come on, kids.
They'll die if you touch them. Okay?

30:18.691 --> 30:19.943
Bring us some good ones!

30:20.026 --> 30:21.861
Don't dump leftovers on this island.

30:21.945 --> 30:24.239
If you touch them and they die,
I can't sell them.

30:24.906 --> 30:28.159
Gwang-rye, stop crying.

30:29.536 --> 30:32.455
You should hurry
and send your precious son to safety.

30:32.539 --> 30:36.167
I hope he finds a wife of noble birth
to bring home.

30:40.129 --> 30:43.174
So you actually fed the chicken a worm.

30:43.258 --> 30:46.261
Wow, you're so good. Really.

30:46.928 --> 30:48.721
Scarily good.

30:52.183 --> 30:53.268
Well,

30:53.893 --> 30:57.188
can I ask you something?

31:00.733 --> 31:04.112
Come on, just think of me as your mother.

31:06.239 --> 31:08.366
Well, was Gwan-sik

31:09.492 --> 31:13.037
really one of the top four in Jeju?

31:14.163 --> 31:17.083
Was he close to winning medals?

31:18.668 --> 31:22.589
He probably would've won one by now
if he hadn't been sidetracked.

31:22.672 --> 31:25.466
He wasn't just any fourth.
He was practically third.

31:26.050 --> 31:28.094
Almost tied for third.

31:29.596 --> 31:31.848
That foolish idiot.

31:33.057 --> 31:35.226
Do you guys curse
when you talk to each other?

31:35.310 --> 31:38.104
He said he just went
for the free milk and bread.

31:38.187 --> 31:40.773
He never told me he was good.

31:42.108 --> 31:45.945
How can he follow me around for ten years
and never tell me what he likes?

31:46.446 --> 31:49.866
He always let me go on and on
about becoming a poet, but he…

31:50.950 --> 31:52.118
But he…

31:52.201 --> 31:54.412
That's what guys
in the Yang family are like.

31:54.495 --> 31:58.416
They think they're not supposed
to express their opinions.

32:06.841 --> 32:08.009
Ae-sun.

32:09.969 --> 32:10.803
Gwan-sik…

32:14.057 --> 32:15.767
will lose it all if he's with you.

32:16.267 --> 32:19.395
He will lose his dreams and his family.

32:20.688 --> 32:24.484
You know what being alone is like,
don't you?

32:26.569 --> 32:29.405
Don't take everything away from Gwan-sik.

32:29.489 --> 32:32.909
You have to let him live his life
to the fullest.

32:35.286 --> 32:36.412
Ae-sun.

32:40.416 --> 32:41.960
Let him live his life.

32:43.002 --> 32:43.836
Please.

32:45.588 --> 32:46.547
Am I…

32:49.300 --> 32:51.344
standing in his way?

32:52.553 --> 32:53.388
Am I

32:55.098 --> 32:56.599
standing in your way?

33:30.425 --> 33:31.259
Gwan-sik!

33:32.468 --> 33:33.469
Here!

33:34.512 --> 33:36.139
You're going to make it.

33:36.222 --> 33:38.141
I've coached for ten years,

33:38.224 --> 33:39.809
but you're the only one

33:39.892 --> 33:42.937
who actually ran 100 laps
just because you were told to.

33:43.438 --> 33:46.858
Your mom sells fish
to support your studies on the mainland.

33:46.941 --> 33:50.069
So let's train hard and win a gold medal.

33:50.153 --> 33:51.571
Once you win a gold medal,

33:52.071 --> 33:55.033
you'll forget what she even looks like.

33:55.783 --> 33:57.785
-You know those gold medals?
-Yeah?

33:58.286 --> 33:59.412
They aren't pure gold.

34:01.330 --> 34:02.165
What?

34:04.459 --> 34:07.211
Why work so hard for something
that's not real gold?

34:07.712 --> 34:08.963
I don't need one anymore.

34:09.047 --> 34:10.506
Is your life over or what?

34:10.590 --> 34:13.801
You were the one harping on
about the gold medal and the mainland.

34:13.885 --> 34:15.094
Well, that's because

34:16.596 --> 34:18.681
Ae-sun wished to leave the island.

34:18.765 --> 34:22.268
Does Ae-sun take up most of your life?

34:22.351 --> 34:23.436
My whole damn life.

34:24.479 --> 34:25.521
Get off.

34:25.605 --> 34:28.900
I only ran 100 laps because of Ae-sun.

34:30.318 --> 34:33.112
Selling fish doesn't pay enough,
and my grades aren't great.

34:33.196 --> 34:35.406
I ran 100 laps in the hope
it'd give me a chance.

34:35.490 --> 34:36.866
What lunatic would run that?

34:38.534 --> 34:39.786
Get off, you punk.

34:39.869 --> 34:43.414
The truth is, I actually hate athletics.

34:43.498 --> 34:44.332
What?

34:44.415 --> 34:46.501
It's not for me.
I can't place better than fourth.

34:46.584 --> 34:48.169
Even if they gave me a box of gold…

34:50.671 --> 34:52.215
I would only do it for Ae-sun.

34:53.549 --> 34:57.011
You crazy bastard.
Then why are you going to Seoul right now?

34:59.097 --> 35:00.973
You have to leave so I can live my life.

35:02.058 --> 35:05.770
You have to leave so I can live my life.

35:23.579 --> 35:25.248
I'm a pretty modern guy.

35:27.750 --> 35:29.669
I'm open-minded, so I can overlook it.

35:31.212 --> 35:33.631
No other family
would have shown you mercy.

35:37.802 --> 35:40.346
How dare that nobody
speak to me like that!

35:40.429 --> 35:41.722
Goddamn it.

35:42.473 --> 35:45.685
His family runs a fish store
that's about the size of a booger?

35:46.185 --> 35:49.147
He doesn't even own anything,
the impudent little punk.

35:49.230 --> 35:50.565
It's bigger than a booger.

35:51.774 --> 35:55.027
-What?
-It's definitely bigger than your boogers.

35:55.111 --> 35:57.488
Goddamn it. You think
you can disrespect a grown-up

35:57.572 --> 35:59.615
just because I've been nice to you?

35:59.699 --> 36:01.909
Why is a grown-up marrying a child, then?

36:01.993 --> 36:04.120
Goddamn it. Hey, you little brat!

36:04.203 --> 36:05.663
Don't speak to me rudely.

36:06.164 --> 36:08.374
Listen, wake up.

36:08.457 --> 36:10.543
I don't think you grasp the situation.

36:11.127 --> 36:13.796
I might be paying your tuition.
Don't tell me how to speak.

36:13.880 --> 36:16.883
Am I marrying a perfect girl
from a wealthy family?

36:16.966 --> 36:18.384
I don't want your money.

36:19.594 --> 36:20.595
I don't want it.

36:22.805 --> 36:23.806
Really?

36:24.807 --> 36:27.059
Wait, are you serious, miss?

36:29.353 --> 36:30.438
What about college?

36:31.606 --> 36:35.109
What about becoming a poet?
What about the mainland?

36:37.195 --> 36:39.739
I should only rely on my family.

36:45.703 --> 36:49.123
Aren't you marrying me to go to college?

36:50.249 --> 36:51.334
Why else would you?

36:54.086 --> 36:55.630
Why else would you marry me?

36:57.590 --> 36:58.507
I don't have…

37:00.509 --> 37:01.510
anywhere to go.

37:03.721 --> 37:04.555
What?

37:06.891 --> 37:08.768
There's nothing else I can do.

37:09.977 --> 37:11.562
I'm going to do it all.

37:13.064 --> 37:14.398
I'm going to do all of it.

37:14.899 --> 37:16.859
I'll be the chief of the fishing co-op.

37:16.943 --> 37:19.570
I'm also going to be
the president five times.

37:19.654 --> 37:21.489
All right, go on. Do it!

37:21.989 --> 37:24.408
Let's make a king
out of one of our haenyeo crew.

37:24.951 --> 37:28.079
I wonder why she wasn't born as a boy.

37:28.162 --> 37:33.334
How is it that such a little girl
has been gifted with so much potential?

37:33.417 --> 37:37.338
If she has such great potential,
she should run for president.

37:38.381 --> 37:41.008
Go ahead.
You already have eight votes from us.

37:42.718 --> 37:43.552
Nine votes.

37:45.763 --> 37:47.098
That's right! Nine.

37:47.974 --> 37:49.934
What score did you get in math?

37:51.227 --> 37:52.728
What do you want to become?

37:56.482 --> 37:58.234
Don't even ask him!

37:59.652 --> 38:00.569
The First Lady.

38:03.823 --> 38:04.949
The First Lady.

38:08.077 --> 38:10.538
-My goodness, kid.
-Look who's got a crush!

38:27.888 --> 38:30.850
I'm getting married
because I have nowhere else to go.

38:31.726 --> 38:33.686
Even if I died, I'd have nowhere to go.

38:33.769 --> 38:36.981
They say living on a pile of dog crap
is better than dying, so…

38:37.481 --> 38:38.649
I'm a pile of dog crap?

38:40.026 --> 38:41.986
Can you just hire me?

38:42.069 --> 38:44.905
I'll be a maid or a babysitter
and make it worth your while.

38:47.325 --> 38:49.035
Hey, listen.

38:49.118 --> 38:52.621
All the housework will be free
if I get a wife, so why would I?

38:53.331 --> 38:54.248
Why would I do that?

38:55.207 --> 38:58.502
As the queen of love,
you may have dreamed of a passionate love,

38:58.586 --> 39:00.421
but I'm just looking for a spouse.

39:00.504 --> 39:04.342
I want a docile daughter-in-law for my mom
and a frugal mother for my children.

39:04.842 --> 39:05.760
For God's sake!

39:10.222 --> 39:14.143
I only met my ex-wife five times
before we got married.

39:14.226 --> 39:15.603
People live like that.

39:15.686 --> 39:18.481
You just have to make a fuss over it,
don't you?

39:19.982 --> 39:22.985
Hey, wait!
Just use the cheapest fabrics here.

39:34.288 --> 39:36.415
Anyway, tell me this.

39:38.042 --> 39:39.418
You spent the night with him?

39:54.016 --> 39:55.643
That crazy little brat!

39:57.603 --> 39:59.313
If she hadn't run that day…

40:00.314 --> 40:01.816
If she hadn't run…

40:03.109 --> 40:06.195
Gyeong-ok, let's go home.

40:11.450 --> 40:13.869
This damn rain. It's bucketing down!

40:15.329 --> 40:17.581
Let's just say it was a rough patch.

40:18.416 --> 40:21.085
Out of sight, out of mind.

40:21.168 --> 40:22.837
Out of mind?

40:23.546 --> 40:27.508
Then why do the Cowherd and Weaver Girl's
tears still rain down on us today?

40:27.591 --> 40:28.801
Gwan-sik!

40:30.219 --> 40:31.470
Gwan-sik!

40:33.013 --> 40:34.598
Gwan-sik!

40:37.268 --> 40:38.727
Where are you going?

40:40.771 --> 40:41.981
Where are you going?

40:43.691 --> 40:46.402
How can you just leave me here?

40:47.278 --> 40:48.112
That's right.

40:48.195 --> 40:49.029
Gwan-sik!

40:49.113 --> 40:51.073
How can a young heart resist love?

40:51.157 --> 40:52.867
Yang Gwan-sik!

40:53.451 --> 40:54.785
Yang Gwan-sik!

40:56.954 --> 40:58.914
Hey, Yang Gwan-sik!

41:00.749 --> 41:02.918
Wow, that is loud.

41:07.381 --> 41:08.549
Ae-sun!

41:11.302 --> 41:14.221
Ae-sun! You're going to fall over.

41:14.722 --> 41:16.807
Come here. Aren't you adorable?

41:17.808 --> 41:19.560
Mommy, I want a candy.

41:29.820 --> 41:31.280
Yang Gwan-sik!

41:32.740 --> 41:34.658
Yang Gwan-sik!

41:37.953 --> 41:39.830
Yang Gwan-sik!

41:45.961 --> 41:47.171
Yang Gwan-sik.

41:47.963 --> 41:49.381
Yang Gwan-sik.

41:50.799 --> 41:52.593
Yang Gwan-sik!

41:58.098 --> 42:00.601
Don't go!

42:02.102 --> 42:03.771
Please don't go.

42:16.200 --> 42:17.952
That damn girl is a real pain.

42:19.036 --> 42:20.329
Stop being so obnoxious!

42:20.412 --> 42:22.289
Why don't you stop being so nosy?

42:23.415 --> 42:24.500
Let her be.

42:25.125 --> 42:26.585
Let her yell and scream.

42:35.553 --> 42:37.596
Why do you take everything from me?

42:39.181 --> 42:42.351
Why do you only take everything
that belongs to me?

42:47.398 --> 42:48.649
Mom.

42:51.277 --> 42:52.570
Mom.

42:58.325 --> 42:59.785
Mom!

43:03.664 --> 43:06.208
Man, what's going on?

43:06.792 --> 43:08.586
Is the Dragon King holding us back?

43:08.669 --> 43:10.087
Why is the wind against us?

43:10.588 --> 43:12.881
Damn it. Hey!

43:14.174 --> 43:15.593
The wind is against us.

43:15.676 --> 43:17.094
Turn this boat around.

43:17.177 --> 43:18.679
-Turn it around!
-We're at sea!

43:18.762 --> 43:19.805
Please turn it around!

43:19.888 --> 43:21.181
Please turn back!

43:21.849 --> 43:23.183
You have to turn around!

43:23.684 --> 43:24.768
Get out of here!

43:25.519 --> 43:28.647
Please turn around for just a second!

43:31.525 --> 43:32.818
Get off me!

43:33.444 --> 43:34.403
Wait! Please!

43:34.486 --> 43:36.947
Why is that little punk on my boat again?

43:37.906 --> 43:38.782
The boat, sir!

43:38.866 --> 43:40.159
Excuse me, Captain!

43:41.035 --> 43:42.620
You have to turn around.

43:42.703 --> 43:45.623
Gwan-sik!
You won't die without her, will you?

43:46.624 --> 43:48.250
Will you die? You fool!

43:56.050 --> 43:59.386
If she hadn't run that day…

44:01.889 --> 44:03.390
If she hadn't run…

44:03.974 --> 44:05.726
You're shattering their lives.

44:05.809 --> 44:08.520
Don't you know
what happened to Romeo and Juliet?

44:09.229 --> 44:12.066
A broken heart doesn't take a life.

44:12.566 --> 44:15.903
Once the boat sets sail,
they're in the hands of the Dragon King.

44:15.986 --> 44:18.197
What's the point of her draining herself?

44:18.781 --> 44:19.698
Let's go.

44:20.366 --> 44:23.243
Ae-sun, let's go.
I'll cook you a pork dish.

44:23.327 --> 44:25.079
Pork is better than a boy?

44:26.288 --> 44:27.414
My goodness.

44:27.498 --> 44:29.291
Oh my goodness.

44:30.125 --> 44:32.002
If she hadn't run that day…

44:32.086 --> 44:34.213
Did someone just fall overboard?

44:35.297 --> 44:36.548
Did someone just…

44:36.632 --> 44:40.177
Mommy, brother go splash.

44:40.260 --> 44:41.261
What?

44:41.345 --> 44:44.181
Brother just go splash.

44:48.977 --> 44:51.689
"A broken heart doesn't take a life"?

44:51.772 --> 44:54.024
It just drove a young man
to jump overboard!

44:56.151 --> 44:57.528
Oh no, Mother.

45:06.912 --> 45:11.417
If she hadn't run that day…

45:15.087 --> 45:17.464
Look! Is that a whale or what?

45:18.298 --> 45:20.217
Something is rushing this way!

45:25.973 --> 45:27.599
If she hadn't run that day,

45:29.101 --> 45:32.396
could she have stopped the destiny
that was rushing toward her?

45:43.449 --> 45:44.992
U-turn!

45:46.076 --> 45:47.369
U-turn!

45:49.455 --> 45:52.082
All the way, Gwan-sik!

46:06.764 --> 46:09.183
Of all the sports,
you just had to teach him to swim!

46:11.143 --> 46:14.271
We should send him
to North Korea as an agent!

46:20.778 --> 46:24.490
Destiny has always been sassy,
just like that.

46:59.316 --> 47:00.526
Goodness me!

47:07.074 --> 47:08.116
Are you okay?

47:15.833 --> 47:18.168
I have to pay for these clothes!

47:19.002 --> 47:21.630
I have money.

47:24.383 --> 47:26.593
-What did that man say?
-I don't know.

47:26.677 --> 47:28.929
All he does is gobble up sugar cubes.

47:44.903 --> 47:46.238
Goodness gracious.

47:50.701 --> 47:53.287
This is better
than the Cowherd and the Weaver Girl.

47:55.998 --> 47:58.375
You know, the thing is,

47:58.458 --> 48:02.880
even the heavens couldn't separate
the Cowherd and the Weaver Girl.

48:04.131 --> 48:08.385
Because they had to let the couple meet
on the seventh day of the seventh month.

48:08.969 --> 48:10.721
Your husband couldn't do it either.

48:12.681 --> 48:14.725
No one can stop young love.

48:30.115 --> 48:31.325
Did you know?

48:32.868 --> 48:34.369
Your parents eloped at night.

48:36.038 --> 48:36.872
Eloped at night?

48:38.081 --> 48:39.708
Your auntie is drunk again.

48:40.959 --> 48:42.711
They caused a total ruckus.

48:42.794 --> 48:45.923
All the seas between Jeju and Busan
were stirred up.

48:46.006 --> 48:48.258
Gyeong-ok,
you're confused again from drinking.

48:48.342 --> 48:51.011
Your mother eloped at night, not me.

48:51.094 --> 48:52.679
But the funny part

48:52.763 --> 48:54.765
is what happened in Busan.

48:54.848 --> 48:56.141
Go home now.

48:56.224 --> 48:57.184
Time to get up.

48:57.684 --> 49:00.395
-What happened in Busan?
-They were caught in two days.

49:00.479 --> 49:02.272
-Enough!
-So how…

49:02.356 --> 49:06.568
All right, drink some water and sober up.

49:07.194 --> 49:11.406
Hey, can you call Gyeong-ok's husband?

49:11.490 --> 49:13.367
Busan worked wonders, I tell you.

49:13.450 --> 49:15.160
-You're a true blessing.
-Gyeong-ok!

49:15.243 --> 49:17.496
Do I have to call your husband over?

49:17.579 --> 49:18.622
Come on!

49:18.705 --> 49:20.582
You arrived earlier than expected.

49:22.334 --> 49:24.670
You were born eight months
after the wedding,

49:24.753 --> 49:26.797
even though they were caught in two days.

49:28.840 --> 49:31.176
That's why Busan worked wonders.

49:31.259 --> 49:32.678
You're such a blessing.

49:34.096 --> 49:36.723
That's why your hometown
is Busan, not Jeju.

49:39.226 --> 49:41.103
Blame it on spring.

49:42.521 --> 49:44.564
Spring has a way of getting to people.

49:45.732 --> 49:47.567
Spring in Jeju

49:48.235 --> 49:49.736
has always arrived early

49:50.737 --> 49:52.614
and has been exceptionally sassy.

49:55.742 --> 49:57.202
I think

49:58.078 --> 50:00.414
we should have maybe three kids.

50:00.497 --> 50:03.166
I think three would be perfect.

50:03.250 --> 50:06.253
So, if we're going to pay

50:06.878 --> 50:08.839
for the education of all three,

50:08.922 --> 50:12.134
we have to be very strategic
about how we live.

50:14.553 --> 50:16.263
Have you heard of General MacArthur?

50:17.472 --> 50:19.016
So, strategically,

50:20.142 --> 50:22.394
we should have a daughter first,

50:22.477 --> 50:23.812
then a son--

50:23.895 --> 50:25.105
No time to waste, then.

50:26.273 --> 50:27.107
What?

50:31.028 --> 50:31.862
No time.

50:45.792 --> 50:48.837
Were you throwing a wild circus in there?

50:48.920 --> 50:52.007
How did you even manage
to break the fan on the wall?

50:53.800 --> 50:58.555
Even my mom thinks
Yang Gwan-sik and Oh Ae-sun broke the fan.

50:59.056 --> 51:01.850
Hey, go home. You little brat.

51:01.933 --> 51:02.851
Go now!

51:03.518 --> 51:06.229
I wondered why they called you "Dia"
before you were born.

51:06.313 --> 51:09.733
It turns out they drank Dia soju
in Busan before they--

51:10.859 --> 51:12.736
If you're drunk, just go, you brat.

51:12.819 --> 51:15.489
You're the ones who went to Busan.
Why take it out on me?

51:15.572 --> 51:18.658
You're the one
who came into my home and ate chicken.

51:19.618 --> 51:20.952
Go home now!

51:21.036 --> 51:22.871
There's some left. Don't tell me to go!

51:22.954 --> 51:24.623
We'll pack it for you to go. Okay?

51:24.706 --> 51:26.666
Put your jacket on. Come on.

51:26.750 --> 51:27.584
Go.

51:34.883 --> 51:36.676
Geum-myeong. Look over here.

51:37.260 --> 51:39.221
One, two, three!

51:43.266 --> 51:46.269
I didn't know a person's head
could be so round.

51:46.353 --> 51:47.646
Are you happy?

51:48.146 --> 51:50.315
I didn't know you could smile like that.

51:51.066 --> 51:53.485
Oh my goodness.

51:53.568 --> 51:54.820
Is she that adorable?

51:54.903 --> 51:57.280
She is. An adorable rascal.

51:58.365 --> 52:00.951
A rascal that held her mother back.

52:08.208 --> 52:11.002
Don't be silly.
Who cares about college now?

52:11.086 --> 52:14.548
I have the whole world right here
in my arms.

52:15.382 --> 52:19.302
You're my nostalgia now, aren't you? Huh?

52:24.558 --> 52:26.560
At the National Sports Festival,

52:26.643 --> 52:29.271
a swimmer who wore boxers
instead of swimming trunks

52:29.354 --> 52:32.691
won first place
in the 400 m and 1,500 m freestyle.

52:33.859 --> 52:36.236
Jo O-ryeon, who burst onto the scene,

52:36.319 --> 52:42.409
expressed his ambitious desire to win
the gold medal at the Bangkok Asian Games.

52:51.668 --> 52:52.586
Are you sad

52:53.795 --> 52:55.839
you couldn't be like Jo O-ryeon?

53:00.302 --> 53:03.430
Who cares about a gold medal
when I've got my golden girl?

53:05.182 --> 53:07.309
She is my dream now.

53:09.644 --> 53:13.481
The spring of their lives
flew by in a heartbeat.

53:13.982 --> 53:15.942
FLAG
THIS IS A SILENT OUTCRY

53:16.026 --> 53:17.235
At the age of 18,

53:18.069 --> 53:20.447
my mom, who had lost her own mom,
became a mother.

53:22.741 --> 53:24.034
At the age of 19,

53:24.743 --> 53:27.996
my dad got his golden girl
instead of a gold medal.

53:28.496 --> 53:31.666
Think she'll be a soccer player?
Look at her legs.

53:32.417 --> 53:36.046
I hope she'll be a teacher.
A literature teacher.

53:38.715 --> 53:41.426
-I wonder what she'll be.
-I know, right?

53:44.429 --> 53:47.974
Their spring wasn't a season
to foster dreams

53:48.808 --> 53:50.435
but to break them.

53:56.900 --> 53:59.110
And they did so willingly.

54:01.404 --> 54:06.201
GEUM-MYEONG, OUR ETERNAL NOSTALGIA
MAY 4, 1969

54:07.535 --> 54:10.247
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

54:10.330 --> 54:13.250
Hello, is it okay
if I ask you a few questions?

54:13.750 --> 54:17.462
So you're here to see the flowers today.
How do you feel about them?

54:18.922 --> 54:21.007
The flowers remind me of my first love.

54:21.091 --> 54:23.927
-First love. Of course.
-Go live with her, then.

54:25.637 --> 54:27.472
Hye-ran. That's dirty.

54:27.555 --> 54:29.975
Well, thank you for the interview.

54:30.058 --> 54:31.726
-Hye-ran. It's dirty.
-Okay, then.

54:31.810 --> 54:33.895
Let's interview a few other citizens.

54:33.979 --> 54:37.023
Hello. You must be newlyweds.

54:42.028 --> 54:45.949
These aren't my grandmother's.
They're really mine.

54:46.032 --> 54:48.410
Your first birthday ring
is your mom's, not yours.

54:48.493 --> 54:51.246
But I really want to give her a ring.

54:51.871 --> 54:53.248
You're so tiresome.

54:55.959 --> 54:57.794
Don't look at me like that.

54:58.795 --> 55:00.380
I actually snuck out.

55:02.215 --> 55:03.466
By dawn tomorrow, could--

55:03.550 --> 55:06.553
So you want me to come to work
at dawn because of you?

55:14.144 --> 55:15.478
Fine, leave them here.

55:18.398 --> 55:20.692
Who would live with a man without a ring?

55:29.993 --> 55:32.078
Is the restroom clean?

55:32.162 --> 55:33.038
Clean?

55:33.621 --> 55:34.539
Yeah.

55:35.457 --> 55:36.499
It's usable.

55:42.464 --> 55:44.382
A new ring and a new dress.

55:45.091 --> 55:47.427
This must be a top celebrity's wedding.

55:51.264 --> 55:52.390
Do you really want it?

55:52.974 --> 55:54.851
Is this a wedding or a fashion show?

55:55.602 --> 55:57.479
You should just rent formal wear.

55:57.562 --> 55:58.480
Seriously.

55:58.563 --> 55:59.564
Wear it.

56:00.148 --> 56:01.775
Wear anything you want.

56:01.858 --> 56:04.903
Why not wear your top hat
and strut in a parade?

56:04.986 --> 56:06.404
Pick whatever you want.

56:06.905 --> 56:08.239
For crying out loud.

56:09.699 --> 56:10.575
You like it?

56:12.243 --> 56:13.119
Yeah.

56:13.203 --> 56:15.038
Do you guys want to move out?

56:15.121 --> 56:17.040
If you have the money, just go.

56:17.791 --> 56:19.167
Should I put my hair up?

56:20.835 --> 56:23.755
Does my hair look better up or down?

56:24.714 --> 56:25.757
What?

56:25.840 --> 56:27.008
My hair.

56:27.092 --> 56:29.344
Does it look prettier up or down?

56:32.472 --> 56:33.598
Actually…

56:33.681 --> 56:34.516
Yeah?

56:35.934 --> 56:37.018
Don't you think

56:38.186 --> 56:39.312
you might regret it

56:40.313 --> 56:41.564
in the future?

56:42.399 --> 56:43.233
Why?

56:45.110 --> 56:47.028
I just think it might be…

56:50.115 --> 56:52.659
embarrassing, and…

56:56.496 --> 56:59.958
Do you even know anything about fashion?
Do you know who André Kim is?

57:00.542 --> 57:01.376
No, I don't.

57:04.254 --> 57:06.923
If you have the means, please move out!

57:07.006 --> 57:08.216
This is so annoying.

57:12.303 --> 57:15.807
By the way,
can we have quail noodle soup after this?

57:15.890 --> 57:19.060
You had it just yesterday,
you little piggy.

57:26.317 --> 57:27.277
You look beautiful.

57:31.364 --> 57:34.367
Mom, why did you wear a hat like that?

57:34.993 --> 57:36.744
Was it some kind of dare?

01:00:25.246 --> 01:00:29.250
"THE SAME SKY, THE SAME STARS,
ETCHED IN THE SAME HEARTS."

01:00:36.924 --> 01:00:39.135
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
